    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n22979" root="شمر" body-key="$">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَاةٌ شَامِرٌ</span></b> , and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَامِرَةٌ</span>, <i>A ewe</i> or <i>she-goat, having
her udder drawn up to her belly:</i> (S, K:) an
epithet having no verb. (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَفَةٌ شَامِرَةٌ</span>, and
↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُتَشَمِّرَةٌ</span></b> , <i>A contracted lip.</i> (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لِثَةٌ شَامِرَةٌ</span>,
(A, K,) and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُتَشَمِّرَةٌ</span></b> , (K,) or ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُشَمِّرَةٌ</span></b> , (so in a
copy of the A,) <i>A gum cleaving to the roots of
the teeth.</i> (A, K.)

